Z||000008||deceler8||12-10-2000||12:27 PM||||If you're not using it yet, change to Mobil 1 0W-30...the best thing to happen in cold parts of the country since the heated garage...<P>I've never noticed it to increase oil consumption or leakage, and have used it year round in several cars. Actually, probably frees up a few HP as it flows so much better than even 5W-30.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-10-2000||12:43 PM||||Just a quick note, Cars are not affected by wind chill. But -37C is DANG COLD!||||reg||1
Z||000010||StuGood||12-10-2000||01:49 PM||||Oreif is right about the wind chill - that only affects how <B>fast</B> a (sleeping) car gets cold soaked (down to the same temp. as the air).  <P>Actually, wind chill <B>can</B> cause starting difficulties - such as when your hands are shaking so much, you can't manage to get the key into the ignition switch   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> !<P>----------------------------------------<BR>So, AkursedX, you're saying it isn't so cold there, it's really just Erie? <BR>  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 12-10-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000011||AkursedX||12-10-2000||01:57 PM||||Wow, you guys have made me feel alot better!  Here in Buffalo, it has only gotten down to about 14 degrees or so.  It doesn't get real cold here till the lake freezes over, but instead, we just get a ton of snow! *mad* *mad*  <BR>I'm just glad I have a winter car.  I would cry if I had to put my Fiero through all of the salt on these roads!||||reg||6
