Z||000037||Raydar||12-17-2000||10:35 PM||||Atlanta checking in, again.<BR>Looks like I shot my mouth off, earlier.<BR>Yesterday evening at 7:30 it was 60*F. By 10:30, it had dropped to 45*. By this morning there was snow on the ground. Going down to upper teens tonight. Maybe some snow tomorrow night - Tuesday morning. Looks like we might actually have winter (relatively speaking) this year. <BR>Actually, I don't mind these temps too much.<BR>We need a good long cold snap. Maybe it'll kill some of the bugs. We also need rain. Lots of it. Hopefully, not at the same time, though. We <I>don't</I> need any ice storms, which is what we usually get.<BR>Last year, I don't think the temp dropped below freezing more than 5-6 nights, total. Strange.  <BR>And, no. I <I>don't</I> envy you good people that live North of here. I recognize that what I call "cold" here, you commonly refer to as "fall".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>But the tradeoff is, you get to watch our silly asses freak out over 2" of snow predicted, and strip the grocery stores like a swarm of locusts. <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000038||My7Fieros||12-17-2000||11:15 PM||||LOL Radar! Same situation here w/ the grocery store thing! <BR><B>HOWEVER...</B>, its gotten even COLDER since my last post. And last night (the 16th), it SNOWED! Only alittle over an inch, but snow in Memphis BEFORE Christmas is litterally unheard of here. To top that off, the temp never gets over mid 30's for highs all week this week, AND they're making an early call for SEVERAL inches of snow on Saturday night and Christmas Eve! Now <B>THATS</B> Christmas weather! <B>NOT</B> that 65 degree crap we had last year.<BR>They're saying that this could be the coldest winter Memphis has had in 30 years..it already is! And its not even winter yet! <BR>(I actually really like it, but my poor Fieros dont lol)||||reg||1
